r","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record for Decatur County runs 75 years, from 1951 to 2025. On the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 9 grids, October to November came in under 90% of normal in 40 of those years, and it is the driest pair at 5.59 inches normal. In 2025, September to October came in at 28% of normal and October to November at 31% on the middle of the grids. Every grid&rsquo;s driest year was 1954, and grid 13381 got down to 51% that year.</p>"}
